//? Title: Damerau–Levenshtein: Unrestricted Byte Edits, Actual Tables and Executable Witnesses
//? Subtitle: CA to ABC, the original five pairs, a computed OSA counterexample and checked quadratic work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An adjacent transposition joins insertion, deletion and substitution as a
unit-cost byte edit. The unrestricted Damerau–Levenshtein distance minimizes
over any sequence of these operations. We begin with CA→AC→ABC: a native
shortest script transposes the first two bytes and then inserts B into the
already transposed region. The original five string pairs are retained,
with actual Levenshtein, restricted optimal-string-alignment (OSA) and
unrestricted results. Complete Lowrance–Wagner traces expose prefix values,
last occurrences, all four candidates and deterministic choices. Native
script expansion and checked replay turn the distance into an executable
witness. We derive the recurrence, distinguish OSA's failed triangle
inequality from the unrestricted metric, and measure rectangular table work.
All semantics are literal bytes, including NUL and UTF-8 encodings, with
explicit geometry, candidate arithmetic and complete resource limits.
)

\toc

> Two edits that reuse the transposed region

The unrestricted distance from CA to ABC is two: transpose CA into AC, then
insert B at current position one. OSA returns three because its local
transposition restriction cannot combine these edits in the same region.
The program obtains both operations from the actual native traceback and
replays them through the core byte-edit API; the intermediate strings and
arrow labels are computed from that script.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/damerau_script.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::damerau_levenshtein_trace("CA","ABC");
  const auto edits=dm::algorithms::damerau_edit_script(t);const auto osa=dm::algorithms::optimal_string_alignment_distance(t.source,t.target);
  if(t.distance!=2 || edits.size()!=2 || osa!=3) return 1;
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"match","substitute","insert","erase","transpose"};
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(80,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2.3;box.height=1.2;box.font_size=24;box.fill={219,234,254};
  std::string state=t.source;d.node("0",{0,0},state,box);
  std::print("| edit | operation | current position | expected bytes | replacement bytes | resulting string |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<edits.size();++k) {
    const auto& e=edits[k];state=dm::algorithms::apply_byte_edits(state,{e});
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k+1,names[static_cast<std::size_t>(e.kind)],e.position,e.before.empty()?"empty":e.before,e.after.empty()?"empty":e.after,state);
    box.fill={220,252,231};d.node(std::to_string(k+1),{4.5*(k+1),0},state,box)
     .edge(std::to_string(k),std::to_string(k+1),std::format("{} at {}",names[static_cast<std::size_t>(e.kind)],e.position));
  }
  if(state!=t.target) return 1;
  d.text({4.5,2},std::format("Unrestricted byte distance: {} executable unit edits",t.distance),23)
   .text({4.5,-2},std::format("Same pair: OSA {}; unrestricted DL {}",osa,t.distance),21)
   .save_svg("build/damerau_script.svg");
  const auto& c=t.cells.back();
  std::print("\nReplayed target {}; unrestricted distance {}; OSA {}; previous cross-match positions ({},{}); bridge candidate {}.\n",state,t.distance,osa,c.last_source,c.last_target,c.transposition);
}
```
