\caption(Nested markers retain overlapping results: large red Levenshtein points, orange OSA points and smaller blue DL points. The last pair distinguishes the restricted and unrestricted methods.)
\alttext(Four pairs have Levenshtein two and both transposition-aware values one. CA versus ABC has Levenshtein and OSA three, while unrestricted distance is two.)

> Derive the last-occurrence bridge and inspect its real table

Let D(i,j) be unrestricted distance between the first i source bytes and the
first j target bytes. Boundaries are D(i,0)=i and D(0,j)=j. At positive i,j,
let i₁<i be the last source position containing b_j, and j₁<j the earlier
target position containing a_i. If both exist, the crossed endpoints can be
made adjacent by deleting the intervening source bytes, swapped once, then
separated by inserting the intervening target bytes. That gives the candidate

\[
D(i_1-1,j_1-1)+(i-i_1-1)+1+(j-j_1-1).
\]
\alttext(The bridge starts before the crossed endpoints, deletes the source interior, swaps the adjacent endpoints once and inserts the target interior.)

Lowrance and Wagner prove that a minimum-cost script has a suitable canonical
trace when 2T≥I+D for transposition, insertion and deletion costs. Unit costs
satisfy equality. This justifies considering the last-occurrence bridge beside
the three ordinary moves, rather than enumerating arbitrary edit scripts:

\[
D(i,j)=\min\left\{
D(i-1,j-1)+[a_i\ne b_j],\;
D(i,j-1)+1,\;
D(i-1,j)+1,\;
D(i_1-1,j_1-1)+(i-i_1-1)+1+(j-j_1-1)
\right\}.
\]
\alttext(The four candidates are a match or substitution, insertion, deletion, and the last-occurrence transposition bridge; the bridge is absent without both earlier occurrences.)

A 256-entry last-source-row array supplies i₁. Within each current source
row, the last earlier matching target column supplies j₁. Both are captured
before the current equality update; the source row is recorded only after
the entire row finishes. The implementation's sentinel table H has an extra
row and column, with D(i,j)=H(i+1,j+1). Its finite marker U=n+m and clipped
candidate arithmetic avoid wrapping size_t sums. For positive i,j, the
winning value is at most max(i,j)≤max(n,m)<U, so clipping candidates at U and
assigning U to an unavailable bridge cannot change the minimum. Empty cases
have only boundary values, including the all-zero empty/empty case.

For CA→ABC, cell (2,3) sees i₁=j₁=1. The bridge starts at D(0,0)=0, deletes
zero source bytes, transposes once and inserts the one interior target byte
B: 0+0+1+1=2. Each other candidate is three. The following grid reads ordinary
prefix values from the actual sentinel table through the checked native
accessor. It also computes the OSA triangle counterexample.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/damerau_prefix.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::damerau_levenshtein_trace("CA","ABC");const auto& last=t.cells.back();
  if(last.diagonal!=3 || last.insertion!=3 || last.deletion!=3 || last.transposition!=2) return 1;
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(76,1150);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle cell;cell.width=1.25;cell.height=.9;cell.font_size=21;
  std::print("| source prefix | empty | A | AB | ABC |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<=t.source.size();++i) {
    std::print("| {}",i?t.source.substr(0,i):"empty");d.text({-2,-2.*i},i?t.source.substr(0,i):"empty",20);
    for(std::size_t j=0;j<=t.target.size();++j) {
      const auto value=dm::algorithms::damerau_prefix_distance(t,i,j);std::print(" | {}",value);
      cell.fill=i==2 && j==3?dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
      d.node(std::format("{},{}",i,j),{2.*j,-2.*i},std::to_string(value),cell);
      if(!i) d.text({2.*j,1.6},j?t.target.substr(0,j):"empty",20);
    }
    std::print(" |\n");
  }
  cell.width=4;cell.height=3;cell.fill={254,243,199};cell.font_size=19;
  d.node("bridge",{10,-1.5},std::format("cell (2,3)\nprevious C row {}\nprevious A column {}\n0 + 0 + 1 + 1 = {}",last.last_source,last.last_target,last.transposition),cell)
   .text({4.5,3.3},"Actual ordinary prefix distances; the green cell uses a bridge",22)
   .text({4.5,-6},"The displayed 3 x 4 prefix grid is read from the full 4 x 5 sentinel table",19)
   .save_svg("build/damerau_prefix.svg");
  const auto x=dm::algorithms::optimal_string_alignment_distance("CA","AC"),y=dm::algorithms::optimal_string_alignment_distance("AC","ABC"),z=dm::algorithms::optimal_string_alignment_distance("CA","ABC");
  const auto direct=dm::algorithms::damerau_levenshtein_distance("CA","ABC");if(z<=x+y || direct>x+y) return 1;
  std::print("\nOSA triangle: CA->ABC {}, but CA->AC {} plus AC->ABC {} gives {}. Unrestricted direct distance {}.\n",z,x,y,x+y,direct);
  std::print("Last-cell candidates: diagonal {}, insert {}, erase {}, bridge {}; selected value {}.\n",last.diagonal,last.insertion,last.deletion,last.transposition,last.value);
}
